within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01D_CytotoxicAntibioticsAndRelatedSubstances.L01DB01_Doxorubicin;
model Doxorubicin "Doxorubicin — default model: Doxorubicin_Mohmaed2024_reference"
  extends Doxorubicin_Mohmaed2024_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of doxorubicin: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01D_CytotoxicAntibioticsAndRelatedSubstances.L01DB01_Doxorubicin.Doxorubicin_Mohmaed2024_reference\">Doxorubicin_Mohmaed2024_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of doxorubicin in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Doxorubicin_Mohmaed2024_reference</code></li><li><code>Doxorubicin_Choi2021_PD_w</code></li><li><code>Doxorubicin_Dabour2026_PD_gdf15</code></li></ul><h4>About doxorubicin</h4><p>Doxorubicin is a chemotherapy drug used to treat many cancers, including breast and ovarian cancer, various lymphomas, and several leukemias. It is widely used and appears on the WHO essential medicines list; several doxorubicin products are authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q18936\">Wikidata Q18936</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Doxorubicin\">Doxorubicin</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>10/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 86400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Doxorubicin;
